.TH QUANT-DAP 1 "July 2026" "Quant 1.0.0" "Quant Language Tools"
.SH NAME
quant\-dap \- Debug Adapter Protocol server for Quant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quant\-dap
.RB [ \-\-stdlib
.IR dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quant\-dap
implements the Debug Adapter Protocol (DAP) for the Quant language.
It communicates over stdin/stdout using JSON with Content-Length framing
and is intended to be launched automatically by a DAP-capable editor
such as VS Code when the user starts a debug session.
.PP
The adapter compiles the target source file in-process, then runs the
resulting bytecode under a debug-aware VM.
Breakpoints, single-stepping, stack inspection, and variable expansion
are all supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-stdlib " dir"
Path to the Quant standard library directory.
Overrides the
.B QUANT_STDLIB
environment variable and the compiled-in default
.IR /usr/local/share/quant/lib .
.SH PROTOCOL FEATURES
.TP
.B Breakpoints
Line breakpoints in the source file; verified breakpoints are reported
back to the editor immediately.
.TP
.B Step commands
.BR next \ (step\ over),
.BR stepIn \ (step\ into),
and
.BR continue .
.BR stepOut \ is\ treated\ as\ continue .
.TP
.B Stack trace
Full call stack with source file and line number for each frame.
.TP
.B Scopes and variables
Local variables for each stack frame, with recursive expansion of
arrays, dicts, and structs.
.TP
.B Program output
Standard output from the running program is forwarded to the editor
as DAP
.B output
events on the
.I stdout
category.
.TP
.B Compile errors
Type errors and parse failures are reported as DAP
.B output
events on the
.I stderr
category before the session terminates.
.SH LAUNCH CONFIGURATION
For VS Code, add a configuration to
.I .vscode/launch.json:
.PP
.nf
{
  "type": "quant",
  "request": "launch",
  "name": "Debug Quant File",
  "program": "${file}",
  "stopOnEntry": false
}
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B program
Path to the
.I .qa
source file to compile and debug.
.TP
.B stopOnEntry
If
.BR true ,
execution pauses at the first statement.
Defaults to
.BR false .
.TP
.B stdlib
Optional path to the standard library directory, passed to
.B quant\-dap
as
.BR \-\-stdlib .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QUANT_STDLIB
Path to the Quant standard library.
Used when
.B \-\-stdlib
is not given on the command line.
.SH NOTES
.B quant\-dap
is ordinarily started by the editor, not the user.
For VS Code, install the Quant LSP extension and configure a launch
configuration as described above; the extension will launch
.B quant\-dap
automatically when a debug session begins.
.PP
The adapter path can be configured in VS Code via the
.B quant\-lsp.debugAdapterPath
setting.
Leave the setting empty to search
.BR $PATH .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glados (1),
.BR quant\-lsp (1),
.BR glados\-repl (1)
